{"answer": "No. Otto forbids any tool from declaring a customer, company or account identifier, which includes a customer number, in its input schema. `enforceNoCustomerInput` in `apps/api/src/tools/toolAuth.ts` checks each tool's `inputSchema` and throws an error if a property looks like a customer identifier (FR-034). This means a tool that asks the model for one can't register. The customer number comes instead from the verified login token's `customer_number` claim, which `toolAuth.ts` re-verifies on every call. ADR-001 says the customer identifier is never a model-supplied tool input. For example, `get_booking_status` takes only `booking_reference`. A test, `apps/api/test/customerBoundary.test.ts`, checks every registered tool.", "sources": ["apps/api/src/tools/toolAuth.ts", "adrs/ADR-001-tms-authentication.md", "README.md", "specs/support-agent-tms-tool-contract/contracts/get-booking-status.md", "apps/api/src/oauth/customerIdentity.ts"]}
```

